      "question": {
        ":question/id": "7cc5ee70-2b10-5325-a2dc-cd7c11e6d8be",
        ":question/problem": "The birth rate of crocodiles in a river is modeled by $B(t)=6\\cdot {e}^{0.25t}$ crocodiles per year, while the rate of death is modeled by $D(t)=4\\cdot {e}^{0.25t}$ crocodiles per year, where $t$ represents the number of years since the year $2000.$  \n\nWhat was the rate of change of the crocodile population in $2012?$ Round your answer to the nearest integer.",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The rate of change in the crocodile population $t$ years since $2000$ is equal to the birth rate minus the death rate, that is\n\n$$\nB(t)-D(t).\n$$\n\nSince $2012$ is $12$ years after $2000$, we have $t=12.$ Substituting $t=12,$ the rate of change of the crocodile population in the river  in $2012$ was\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(12)-D(12) & =6\\cdot {e}^{0.25(12)}-4\\cdot {e}^{0.25(12)} \\\\  & =6{e}^{3}-4{e}^{3} \\\\  & =2{e}^{3} \\\\  & \u224840.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of the crocodile population in the river in $2012$ is approximately $40$ crocodiles per year.",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
            ":answer-field/id": "68d15ded-f5ea-533d-bc58-1b30eba5bad8",
