  {
    "label": "46629e3f-8b91-52e2-8f67-4405ebbe6de1",
    "record": {
      "knowledge_point": {
        "db_id": 17592186064154,
        "id": "c7df31c9-b27a-5ce2-93c8-178ba96da000",
        "title": "Determining a Rate of Change"
      },
      "question": {
        ":question/id": "46629e3f-8b91-52e2-8f67-4405ebbe6de1",
        ":question/problem": "The growth rate, $G(t)$, of the number of bacteria in a culture can be modeled by the function $G(t)=100\\cdot {2}^{0.5t}$, where $t$ is the time, in hours, since a sample of bacteria was placed in a Petri dish.  What will be the growth rate of the bacteria after $6$ hours?",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The function $G(t)$ models the growth rate for the bacteria $t$ hours since the sample was put in the Petri dish.\n\nThus, the growth rate of the bacteria culture after $6$ hours is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}G(6) & =100\\cdot {2}^{0.5(6)} \\\\  & =100\\cdot {2}^{3} \\\\  & =100\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =800.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the growth rate of the bacteria is $800$ bacteria per hour.",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
