        "title": "Determining a Rate of Change"
      },
      "question": {
        ":question/id": "2f24a112-83bc-5dfc-b8eb-4133c86e6e85",
        ":question/problem": "The birth rate of a herd of elephants in a region in Africa is modeled by the function  $B(t)=500\\cdot {2}^{0.125t}$ while the rate of death is modeled by $D(t)=400\\cdot {3}^{0.125t}.$ In both cases, $t$ represents the number of years since $1990.$  \n\nWhat was the rate of change of the elephant population in that region in $1998?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The  rate of change in the number of elephants  $t$ years since $1990$ is equal to the difference between the two given rates, that is\n\n$$\nB(t)-D(t).\n$$\n\nAs $1998$ is $8$ years after $1990$, we have $t=8.$  Hence, the  rate of change in the elephant population in that region in $1998$ was \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(8)-D(8) & =500\\cdot {2}^{0.125(8)}-400\\cdot {3}^{0.125(8)} \\\\  & =500\\cdot 2-400\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-200.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change in the elephant population was $-200$ elephants per year.",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
